{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You met.</b> The meaning: if You were angry, You would meet the righteous, like the meaning of \"stood in the breach\" (Psalms 106:23). Or the meaning of פגעת will be: You would accept the appeasement of the righteous, like לא אפגע אדם (Isaiah 47:3, 53:12)." "And the meaning of <b>rejoiced</b>: the righteous who rejoiced in You." "<b>In Your ways they remember You.</b> In the ways that You guided [us], to the faithful of house." "<b>[Behold, You…].</b> And now You were angry, You, and we were sinners. Or its meaning: when You were angry, we had already sinned." "<b>In them.</b> On account of the righteous, for forever You put an end to anger." "<b>And saved.</b> And we were being saved; and behold, נושע is in standing time."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 64, :notes {2 "The manuscript reading שהורתנו is corrected by the editor to שהורת; I translate the corrected form, which yields a smoother clause but the transmitted text may intend 'that You guided us.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:57.963003540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}